From b906df0c3d2f8b5b61a24326957a284aa2c827d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:41:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] AI: value "becomes a copy of target land" by its payoff
 (Thespian's Stage + Dark Depths)

For "~ becomes a copy of target <permanent>" (BecomeCopy with the source as
recipient) the target is only read, but anti_self_harm treated the Contextual
effect as harmful and CopyValuePolicy scored only token copies, by creature
value. A land target scored 0 at best, so Thespian's Stage copied opponents'
basic lands (Yama deck lab: 32 copies in 157 games, never Dark Depths; in a
unit test, the opponent's land 19 of 20 times).

- anti_self_harm: a target that every targeting effect only reads as a
  self-copy's source scores 0 (no controller preference).
- copy_value: a self-copy target is scored like a token copy, plus
  zero_counter_state_trigger_payoff: the creature tokens made by the target's
  "when ~ has no <kind> counters" state trigger when the copy has none of
  those counters (CR 707.2 + CR 603.8 + CR 614.12: counters aren't copied
  and the copy never got the target's enters-with counters). For a legendary
  target of its own, the cost is the original lost to the legend rule.
- Legend rule (CR 704.5j): a land whose own such payoff is live is kept over
  a copy that still has its counters, so the Stage copy is kept.
- combo registry: a Thespian's Stage + Dark Depths line, so the tutor scorer
  (which uses near-reachable lines at every difficulty) fetches the missing
  piece when the other is on the battlefield. Not a win by itself.

Tests (policies/tests/land_copy_value.rs): the engine makes Marit Lage when
the copy is kept; over 20 seeds the Easy AI copies Dark Depths (19, opponent's
land 0) and gets Marit Lage (19).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
